Native security relay staging, not a default kernel feature
==========================================================

security_relay.rs is the intended pure transition code for the Native Host's
physical ConnectionSession. It is actively being wired into the real Host;
it is not the retired SecurityInner/SLE wire engine and is not built by the
default Makefile. No allow(dead_code), mock success or weak-key fallback.

Implemented: one prepared/submitted relay, two queued PDUs, exact SDK111 five
byte envelope, immutable controller/generation/lifetime/handle/Grant epoch,
original deadline, pre-submit withdrawal, in-flight reply obligation, and
uncertain transport failure retaining debt/reset requirement. USB success is
not Complete; successful Status is not terminal; no command credit is owned
here. Payloads are bounded and never truncated.

Integration requirements, still MISSING:

* Runtime owns one such object/attempt per physical connection lifetime, not
  per application fd. Reopening/dup must not recreate it or restart a deadline.
  A new attempt on the same connection needs an explicit abort/drain protocol,
  late-message quarantine and a verified barrier; changing local cookies alone
  cannot establish that barrier. Constructor/canonical epoch allocation and
  the sole session table have not yet been connected.
* Host resolves authority under its actual lock and schedule gate, shares its
  existing command credit/reservation, and keeps atomic driver submission under
  these guards. The callback must return error only if never queued. A caller
  supplied Identity is not an independently validated Grant or authorization.
* Driver prepares/validates typed1812; raw metadata admission remains unchanged.
  Explicit0014/000e/0011 decoding/attribution and the265-byte relay RX maximum,
  real reply routing, physical abort/stop/join and reset barriers must be wired.
* Opcode-only firmware completion carries no cookie/generation/lifetime. The
  ticket API rejects local mismatches, but does NOT prove late/duplicate wire
  replies cannot pay a newer same-opcode reservation. Firmware/hardware barrier
  assumptions require dedicated models and VM-only controlled real tests.
* Protocol negotiation, fresh nonces/ECDH, peer proof, Agent, security levels,
  role-bound1c03/1c05 key installation/matching0011 and Bond remain unconnected.
  No authenticated/encrypted state or remote CCC capability may be published.

Exit staging only when the sole Host/Session producer and consumer are wired,
strict builds/regressions and relevant implementation proofs pass, and exact
new VM images preserve real two-device discovery/link/socket/length gates.
Then move this SAME source into the normal module tree; do not maintain a second
verification implementation. All S0-S6 and issue scopes remain open.
